Map:MAPMPAdornRiver/Desc
"The Adorn River flows into the River Isen and helps form the western border of Rohan.\n\n Size: 600 x 400\n Lairs:\n Neutral Structures: 4x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire, 4x Tower"
END

Map:MAPMPAmonAmarth
"Amon Amarth"
END

Map:MAPMPAmonAmarth/Desc
"Amon Amarth, the mountain of fate, is located deep within Mordor. It is also known as Mount Doom.\n\n Size: 433 x 500\n Lairs:\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost"
END

Map:MAPMPAmonSulFortress
"Amon Sul Fortress"
END

Map:MAPMPAmonSulFortress/Desc
"The fortress on the windy hill of Amon Sul was the cornerstone of Arnor's defense against Angmar.\n\n Size: 325 x 275\n Lairs:\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPAnorien
"Anorien"
END

Map:MAPMPAnorien/Desc
"The northwestern territory of Gondor that forms the border between Gondor and Rohan.\n\n Size: 421 x 361\n Lairs: 2x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPArgonath
"Argonath"
END

Map:MAPMPArgonath/Desc
"The two mighty statues along the Anduin River were carved in the likeness of the Gondor Kings, Isildur and Anarion. They marked the northern border of Gondor.\n\n Size: 315 x 370\n Lairs: 4x Goblin Lair, 2x Spider Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire, 4x Tower"
END

Map:MAPMPAzanulbizarValley
"Azanulbizar Valley"
END

Map:MAPMPAzanulbizarValley/Desc
"A great valley lying between the foothills of the mountains around the lake of Kheled-zaram. The final battle of the War of the Dwarves and Orcs took place here.\n\n Size: 370 x 380\n Lairs: 4x Goblin Lair, 4x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPDale
"Dale"
END

Map:MAPMPDale/Desc
"A flourishing city of Men located at the foot of the Lonely Mountain.\n\n Size: 360 x 400\n Lairs: 4x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPDesertofRhun
"Desert of Rhun"
END

Map:MAPMPDesertofRhun/Desc
"A vast desert lying to the south-east of Rhun. Many unprepared travellers lose their way attempting to traverse this rugged region. \n\n Size: 550 x 550\n Lairs: 6x Goblin Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPDruadanForest
"Druadan Forest"
END

Map:MAPMPDruadanForest/Desc
"The Druadan Forest is a pine forest in Gondor, located in Anorien, north of Minas Tirith. The forest is home to mysterious folk known as the Druedain, the Wild Men of the Woods.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 4x Spider Lair, 4x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPDruwaithReef
"Dungeons of Erebor"
END

Map:MAPMPDungeonsOfErebor/Desc
"A vast cavern within the Lonely Mountain where the Dwarves mine their riches and trade with the Men of Dale.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 4x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPEastBight
"East Bight"
END

Map:MAPMPEastBight/Desc
"The indentation on the eastern side of Mirkwood, caused by generations of forestry. Trees now grow sparsely in this area.\n\n Size: 200 x 300\n Lairs:\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost"
END

Map:MAPMPEmynArnen
"Emyn Arnen"
END

Map:MAPMPEmynArnen/Desc
"Green, lush lands in central Gondor, bordering the dark mountains that separate Gondor from Mordor in the east.\n\n Size: 400 x 500\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPErech
"Erech"
END

Map:MAPMPErech/Desc
"Erech II"
END

Map:MAPMPErechII/Desc
"A hill west of Minas Tirith, where in ages past the faithless King of the Mountains swore an oath of fealty to Isildur.\n\n Size: 320 x 320\n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPEredMithrin
"Ered Mithrin"
END

Map:MAPMPEredMithrin/Desc
"Of old the Ered Mithrin had been mined and inhabited by Dwarves of Durin's Folk, but by the Third Age only one Dwarven stronghold remained, standing strong against raiding Dragons from the nearby Withered Heath.\n\n Size: 600 x 500\n Lairs: 4x Warg Lair, 1x Troll Lair, 3x Fire Drake Lair, 1x Destructible Environment\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 1x Inn, 1x Signal Fire, 2x Tower"
END

Map:MAPMPEregion
"Eregion"
END

Map:MAPMPEregion/Desc
"Known also as Hollin, Eregion was a kingdom of the Noldorin Elves in Eriador during the Second Age. It is located near the West Gate of Moria under the shadow of the Hithaeglir.\n\n Size: 350 x 400\n Lairs: 2x Warg Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPErynLaer
"Eryn Laer"
END

Map:MAPMPErynLaer/Desc
"The tall trees of Eryn Laer, the Woods of Song, stand deep in the realm of Lothlorien, the heart of Elvendom in Middle-earth.\n\n Size: 325 x 375\n Lairs: 4x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPEvendim
"Evendim"
END

Map:MAPMPEvendim/Desc
"A lone lake not far from the Shire.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 8x Goblin Lair, 4x Barrow Wight\n Neutral Structures: 4x Outpost, 1x Signal Fire, 8x Shipwright"
END

Map:MAPMPFarHarad
"Far Harad"
END

Map:MAPMPFarHarad/Desc
"Deep in southern Middle-earth, the region of Far Harad is the homeland of the wild Haradrim, loyal servants of Sauron.\n\n Size: 380 x 370\n Lairs: 2x Spider Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPFordsOfHarnen
"Fords of Harnen"
END

Map:MAPMPFordsOfHarnen/Desc
"The river Harnen was a river south of Gondor. South of the Harnen lay the land of Near Harad.\n\n Size: 560 x 450\n Lairs: 4x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPFordsofIsen
"Fords of Isen"
END

Map:MAPMPFordsofIsen/Desc
"Fords of Isen II"
END

Map:MAPMPFordsofIsenII/Desc
"The river Isen passes between Isengard and Helm's Deep. Many travellers journeying to and from the Gap of Rohan cross the mighty river at this shallow point.\n\n Size: 550 x 313\n Lairs: 8x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPFordsOfRohan
"Fords of Rohan"
END

Map:MAPMPFordsOfRohan/Desc
"A peaceful battleground situated between the lands of Rohan and Isengard, separated by the river Isen.\n\n Size: 350 x 375\n Lairs: 2x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPForochel
"Forochel"
END

Map:MAPMPForochel/Desc
"Frozen wastelands in northern Middle-earth. The ancient stronghold of Morgoth, Utumno, was located here.\n\n Size: 500 x 400\n Lairs: 2x Goblin, 4x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 3x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPGatesofMoria
"Gates of Moria"
END

Map:MAPMPGatesofMoria/Desc
"An enormous and very ancient underground complex in north-western Middle-earth that runs through the Misty Mountains.\n\n Size: 400 x 400\n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 1x Inn, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPGreyMountains
"Grey Mountains"
END

Map:MAPMPGreyMountains/Desc
"A northern range of mountains where Goblins and Dwarves have battled for many ages.\n\n Size: 485 x 550\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 2x Fire Drake Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPGorgoroth
"Gorgoroth"
END

Map:MAPMPGorgoroth/Desc
"A hostile and desolate region in Mordor, frequently reshaped through volcanic activities.\n\n Size: 480 x 580\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 4x Troll Lair, 2x Fire Drake Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPHaradOasis
"Harad Oasis"
END

Map:MAPMPHaradOasis/Desc
"A region deep within Harad where precious pools of water can be found.\n\n Size: 400 x 400\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPHarlond
"Harlond"
END

Map:MAPMPHarlond/Desc
"The port and docks of Minas Tirith, where Aragorn and the Army of the Dead came ashore during the battle for Minas Tirith.\n\n Size: 495 x 545\n Lairs: 6x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 3x Outpost, 3x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPHillsofEriador
"Hills of Eriador"
END

Map:MAPMPHillsOfEriador/Desc
"An old battlefield in Eriador where countless skirmishes have occurred throughout the ages.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 8x Goblin Lair, 4x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Outpost, 1x Tower"
END

Map:MAPMPHobbiton
"Hobbiton"
END

Map:MAPMPHobbiton/Desc
"An old village in the central part of the Shire. It is the home of many illustrious Hobbits.\n\n Size: 403 x 400\n Lairs: 4x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPHollin
"Hollin"
END

Map:MAPMPIslandsofValinor
"Islands of Valinor"
END

Map:MAPMPIslandsofValinor/Desc
"A small group of islands at the shores of the Immortal Lands.\n\n Size: 600 x 530\n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire, 4x Shipwright, 2x Tower"
END

Map:MAPMPIthilienHills
"Ithilien Hills"
END

Map:MAPMPIthilienHills/Desc
"A small range of hills in the center of Ithilien, the easternmost province of Gondor.\n\n Size: 500 x 450\n Lairs: 2x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPLanthirLamath
"Lanthir Lamath"
END

Map:MAPMPLanthirLamath/Desc
"Lanthir Lamath was the shimmering, glittering waterfall that ran beside the house of Dior Eluchil in Ossiriand, which formed part of the stream of the River Adurant. \n\n Size: 600 x 600\n Lairs: 6x Spider Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Outpost"
END

Map:MAPMPLorienPlateau
"Lorien Plateau"
END

Map:MAPMPLorienPlateau/Desc
"An area of highland in the Woods of Lothlorien, the fairest forest realm of the Elves remaining in Middle-earth.\n\n Size: 550 x 550\n Lairs: 4x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPMithlondValley
"Mithlond Valley"
END

Map:MAPMPMithlondValley/Desc
"A periphery settlement of the Grey Havens, constructed in a great valley that originates in the Ered Lindon.\n\n Size: 450 x 500\n Lairs: 4x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPMountGram
"Mount Gram"
END

Map:MAPMPMountGram/Desc
"The mountain was long inhabited by a group of Orcs led by Golfimbul. They terrorized some of the inhabitants of eastern Eriador including those of the Shire.\n\n Size: 340 x 340\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPNanduhirion
"Nanduhirion"
END

Map:MAPMPNanduhirion/Desc
"This valley was the site of the decisive battle in the War of the Dwarves and Orcs.\n\n Size: 550 x 450\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 4x Troll Lair, 2x Fire Drake Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Outpost, 1x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPNevrast
"Nevrast"
END

Map:MAPMPNevrast/Desc
"Old Brown Lands"
END

Map:MAPMPOldBrownLands/Desc
"Lands to the east of the River Anduin scorched by Sauron at the end of the Second Age. Once the lush home of the Entwives, this area has been desolate since the battles of the Last Alliance.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 10x Goblin Lair\n Neutral Structures:"
END

Map:MAPMPOldForest
"Old Forest"
END

Map:MAPMPOldForest/Desc
"Standing between the borders of Buckland and Breeland, The Old Forest hides great mystery and danger beneath its dark canopy.\n\n Size: 360 x 310\n Lairs: 4x Spider Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPPathsOfTheDead
"Paths of the Dead"
END

Map:MAPMPPathsOfTheDead/Desc
"A cavernous passageway through the White Mountains running from Dwimorberg in the north to the Morthond Vale in the south.\n\n Size: 230 x 390\n Lairs:\n Neutral Structures:"
END

Map:MAPMPPlainsofRohan
"Plains of Rohan"
END

Map:MAPMPPlainsOfRohan/Desc
"Red Desert of Khand"
END

Map:MAPMPRedDesertofKhand/Desc
"A red desert land which lay to the south-east of Mordor and to the east of Near Harad.\n\n Size: 440 x 440\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:mapmpRingloRiver
"Ringlo River"
END

Map:mapmpRingloRiver/Desc
"A winding river in the central regions of Gondor which served as the boundary between Anfalas to the west and Belfalas to the east.\n\n Size: 500 x 450\n Lairs: 4x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 1x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPRiverLangwell
"River Langwell"
END

Map:MAPMPRiverLangwell/Desc
"The Langwell was one of the rivers of Rhovanion that flowed east from the Misty Mountains into the Anduin. The height of the river depends on the season of the year. Over time the water level rises and falls.\n\n Size: 600 x 20\n Lairs: 4x Spider Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPRiverOfOrodruin
"River of Orodruin"
END

Map:MAPMPRiverOfOrodruin/Desc
"Orodruin, also known as Mount Doom, is a towering volcano in the land of Mordor. Around it, there is an arid plateau that is separated by rivers of lava.\n\n Size: 380 x 340\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 2x Troll Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPRiverRunning
"River Running"
END

Map:MAPMPRiverRunning/Desc
"The River Running, also know as Celduin, is a long river that flows from the Lonely Mountain, down through the vast region of Rhovanion, into the inland Sea of Rhun.\n\n Size: 360 x 420\n Lairs: 1x Goblin Lair, 3x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 1x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPRohanII
"Rohan Fortifications"
END

Map:MAPMPRohanFortifications/Desc
"Rohan is a grassland inhabited by Rohirrim. Before and during the Battle of the Hornburg they had to fight with Dunlendings, men related to the House of Haleth.\n\n Size: 360 x 380\n Lairs: 2x Spider Lair, 2x Troll Lair, 2x Destructible Gates\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPSouthDowns
"South Downs"
END

Map:MAPMPSouthDowns/Desc
"Walking along the East-West Road from Bree to the Weather Hills, one could see the Downs to the south. The Greenway, running through the Andrath, separated the South Downs from the Barrow-downs.\n\n Size: 460 x 460\n Lairs: 6x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 1x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPStaddle
"Staddle"
END

Map:MAPMPStaddle/Desc
"A village in Bree Land, located on the southeastern side of Bree-hill.\n\n Size: 498 x 518\n Lairs: 4x Warg Lair, 4x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPStonewainCanyon
"Stonewain Canyon"
END

Map:MAPMPStonewainCanyon/Desc
"Stonewain Canyon is a road that had been made in ancient days by the Men of Gondor. Theoden used the old canyon as the route to reach Gondor to aid the Men of Minas Tirith.\n\n Size: 550 x 460\n Lairs: 8x Troll Lair, 3x Fire Drake Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Outpost, x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPStonewainValley
"Stonewain Valley"
END

Map:MAPMPStonewainValley/Desc
"This valley was made in the Ancient days by Men as a route from the quarries beneath Nardol to Minas Anor.\n\n Size: 550 x 250\n Lairs: 4x Troll Lair, 2x Fire Drake Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPTombsOfKarna
"Tombs of Karna"
END

Map:MAPMPTombsOfKarna/Desc
"Tyrn Gorthad"
END

Map:MAPMPTyrnGorthad/Desc
"Better known as the Barrow-downs, the ancient burial grounds of the kings of Arnor were corrupted with evil spirits by the Witch-king.\n\n Size: 370 x 320\n Lairs: 7x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPUmbar
"Umbar"
END

Map:MAPMPUmbar/Desc
"This great cape is held by the Black Numenoreans who have long feuded with the Men of Gondor.\n\n Size: 310 x 317\n Lairs: 2x Spider Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Inn, 1x Signal Fire, 4x Shipwright"
END

Map:MAPMPWasteOfForodwaith
"Waste of Forodwaith"
END

Map:MAPMPWasteOfForodwaith/Desc
"A frozen tundra to the far north that makes for an even battleground.\n\n Size: 220 x 390\n Lairs:\n Neutral Structures: 4x Outpost, 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPWeathertop
"Weathertop"
END

Map:MAPMPWeathertop/Desc
"The ancient Tower of Amon Sul was built by the North Kingdom to hold one of their three Palantiri. Destroyed by the armies of Angmar, now all that remains is a ring of broken stonework.\n\n Size: 450 x 415\n Lairs: 8x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Inn, 4x Tower"
END

Map:MAPMPWestfold
"Westmarch"
END

Map:MAPMPWestmarch/Desc
"A land of meadows and rises, between the Tower Hills and the Shire.\n\n Size: 500 x 350\n Lairs: 4x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Inn, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPWildsOfForochel
"Wilds of Forochel"
END

Map:MAPMPWildsOfForochel/Desc
"A wild and treacherous region of Forochel scarcely inhabited by small northmen tribes.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 5x Warg Lair, 5x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPWitheredHeath
"Withered Heath"
END

Map:MAPMPWitheredHeath/Desc
"This desolate region in the Grey Mountains is feared by many to be the breeding ground of dragons.\n\n Size: 400 x 550\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 2x Fire Drake Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPWold
"Wold"
END

Map:MAPMPWold/Desc
"The Wold is the northernmost and least populated part of Rohan. It is a grassy upland plain lying between Fangorn Forest and the Anduin, bordered to the north by the Limlight.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 8x Warg Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Outpost, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPWoodyEnd
"Woody End"
END

Map:MAPMPWoodyEnd/Desc
"Amon Sul"
END

Map:MAPWORANGAmonSul/Desc
"The fortress on the windy hill of Amon Sul housed a palantir until the fortress was destroyed by the Witch-king's army. Later it came to be known as Weathertop.\n\n Size: 325 x 275\n Lairs:\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORANGAngmar
"Angmar"
END

Map:MAPWORANGAngmar/Desc
"The icy northern home of Black Numenoreans, Trolls, and Wolves.\n\n Size: 350 x 350\n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORANGBarrowDowns
"Barrow Downs"
END

Map:MAPWORANGBarrowDowns/Desc
"The ancient burial grounds of the kings of Arnor.\n\n Size: 400 x 350\n Lairs: 4x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Inn"
END

Map:MAPWORANGCarnDum
"Carn Dum"
END

Map:MAPWORANGCarnDum/Desc
"The fortress city built by the Witch-king of Angmar.\n\n Size: 400 x 500\n Lairs:\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 1x Signal Fire, Fortress"
END

Map:MAPWORANGFornost
"Fornost"
END

Map:MAPWORANGFornost/Desc
"The capital city of Arthedain, the northern realm of Arnor. After its destruction it became known as Deadman's Dike and was visited only by Rangers.\n\n Size: 300 x 450\n Lairs:\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire, Fortress"
END

Map:MAPWORANGGundabad
"Mount Gundabad"
END

Map:MAPWORANGGundabad/Desc
"A mountain at the northern end of the Misty Mountains that is a breeding ground for Orcs.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 6x Goblin Lair, 1x Spider Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Inn, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORANGNorthDowns
"North Downs"
END

Map:MAPWORANGNorthDowns/Desc
"A hilly region of Arnor found to the north of Bree and Amon Sul.\n\n Size: 500 x 350\n Lairs: 1x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 1x Inn"
END

Map:MAPWORANGRhudaur
"Rhudaur"
END

Map:MAPWORANGRhudaur/Desc
"The hilly eastern kingdom of Arnor, home to tribes of hillmen.\n\n Size: 500 x 450\n Lairs:\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 1x Inn"
END

Map:MAPWORArnor
"Arnor"
END

Map:MAPWORArnor/Desc
"This was once the realm of the Great North Kingdom of Men.\n\n Size: 400 x 425\n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORBelfalas
"Belfalas"
END

Map:MAPWORBelfalas/Desc
"The eastern coastal section of Gondor that stretches from the mouth of the great river Anduin to the citadel city of Dol Amroth.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 3x Goblin Lair, 3x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Inn, 1x Signal Fire, 4x Shipwright, 1x Tower"
END

Map:MAPWORBlackGate
"Black Gate"
END

Map:MAPWORBlackGate/Desc
"The northern entrance to the lands of Mordor and the site of the final stand-off between good and evil.\n\n Size: 450 x 450\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 2x Fire Drake Lair\n Neutral Structures:"
END

Map:MAPWORBuckland
"Buckland"
END

Map:MAPWORBuckland/Desc
"The Eastern border of the Shire was the home of Merry Brandybuck.\n\n Size: 350 x 350\n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORCairAndros
"Cair Andros"
END

Map:MAPWORCairAndros/Desc
"An old Gondor island fortress on the Anduin River, north of the city of Osgiliath.\n\n Size: 410 x 450\n Lairs: 1x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair, 3x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire, 12x Tower"
END

Map:MAPWORCardolan
"Cardolan"
END

Map:MAPWORCardolan/Desc
"One of the three kingdoms of Arnor, Cardolan lies between the rivers Brandywine and Greyflood (with the Great East road serving as its northern border).\n\n Size: 500 x 400\n Lairs: 4x Warg Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORCarrock
"Carrock"
END

Map:MAPWORCarrock/Desc
"A region along the upper reaches of the great river Anduin, Carrock is named for a rocky river island north of the Old Ford.\n\n Size: 361 x 421\n Lairs: 2x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORCelduin
"Celduin"
END

Map:MAPWORCelduin/Desc
"The settlements along the River Running, which rises from Erebor and flows southward into the Sea of Rhun.\n\n Size: 450 x 465\n Lairs: 4x Troll Lair, 4x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Outpost, 6x Inn, 2x Signal Fire, 4x Shipwright, 2x Tower"
END

Map:MAPWORDagorlad
"Dagorlad"
END

Map:MAPWORDagorlad/Desc
"Also known as the Plain of Victory, Dagorlad is where the War of the Last Alliance took place at the end of the Second Age.\n\n Size: 500 x 480\n Lairs: 6x Goblin Lair, 2x Fire Drake Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 4x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORDeadMarshes
"Dead Marshes"
END

Map:MAPWORDeadMarshes/Desc
"A haunted swampland, lying just outside Mordor. Gollum led Frodo and Sam through these lands on their way to Mount Doom.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 2x Troll Lair, 6x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORDolGuldur
"Dol Guldur"
END

Map:MAPWORDolGuldur/Desc
"Sauron's hilltop stronghold in Mirkwood, now led by his Ringwraiths.\n\n Size: 480 x 480\n Lairs: 8x Spider Lair\n Neutral Structures: 5x Signal Fire, Fortress"
END

Map:MAPWOREnedwaith
"Enedwaith"
END

Map:MAPWOREnedwaith/Desc
"A wide, open land that lies to the west of Rohan.\n\n Size: 450 x 450\n Lairs: 4x Warg Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Inn, 4x Signal Fire, 2x Tower"
END

Map:MAPWORErebor
"Erebor"
END

Map:MAPWORErebor/Desc
"The Dwarven fortress within Mount Erebor is the proud domain of King Dain Ironfoot.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 2x Fire Drake Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 1x Inn, 2x Signal Fire, 6x Tower, Fortress"
END

Map:MAPWOREttenmoors
"Ettenmoors"
END

Map:MAPWORFangorn
"Fangorn"
END

Map:MAPWORFangorn/Desc
"A dark and mysterious forest that is the home of Treebeard and the Ents.\n\n Size: 350 x 350\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPWORForlindon
"Forlindon"
END

Map:MAPWORForlindon/Desc
"The Northern part of the Elf lands of Lindon are bordered by the Blue Mountains and the Great Sea.\n\n Size: 400 x 400\n Lairs: 7x Goblin Lair, 1x Warg Lair 2x Fire Drake Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 1x Signal Fire, 3x Shipwright"
END

Map:MAPWORForodwaith
"Forodwaith"
END

Map:MAPWORForodwaith/Desc
"The northern wastelands that stretch north and east from the Ice Bay of Forochel.\n\n Size: 430 x 450\n Lairs: 4x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Inn, 2x Signal Fire, 4x Tower"
END

Map:MAPWORGapofRohan
"Gap of Rohan"
END

Map:MAPWorGreyHavens
"Grey Havens"
END

Map:MAPWORGreyHavens/Desc
"The Elven harbor from which the Elves of Middle-earth would pass to the West.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 6x Shipwright, 8x Tower"
END

Map:MAPWORHarad
"Harad"
END

Map:MAPWORHarad/Desc
"A barren, desert land that lies south of Mordor. It is the homeland of the Haradrim warriors.\n\n Size: 400 x 400\n Lairs: 7x Goblin Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORHarlindon
"Harlindon"
END

Map:MAPWORHarlindon/Desc
"These Elvish lands are the southern parts of Lindon, lying between the Blue Mountains and the Great Sea.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 4x Goblin Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 2x Inn, 1x Signal Fire, 3x Shipwright, 2x Tower"
END

Map:MAPWORHelmsDeep
"Helm's Deep"
END

Map:MAPWORHelmsDeep/Desc
"This aged stronghold is the site of one of the key battles in the War of the Ring. No enemy had ever defeated the defenders of the walls of the Hornburg.\n\n Size: 400 x 400\n Lairs:\n Neutral Structures: 3x Outpost, Fortress"
END

Map:MAPWORHighPass
"High Pass"
END

Map:MAPWORHighPass/Desc
"A narrow and dangerous pass through the Misty Mountains east of Rivendell.\n\n Size: 400 x 400\n Lairs: 3x Goblin Lair, 3x Spider Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORIsengard
"Isengard"
END

Map:MAPWORIsengard/Desc
"Originally a fortress of Gondor, Isengard was occupied by the corrupted wizard Saruman during the War of the Ring.\n\n Size: 400 x 250\n Lairs: 3x Warg Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, Fortress"
END

Map:MAPWORIthilien
"Ithilien"
END

Map:MAPWORIthilien/Desc
"The fertile, wooded lands that lie between the mountains of Mordor and Gondor.\n\n Size: 300 x 350\n Lairs: 4x Goblin Lair, 1x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORLorien
"Lorien"
END

Map:MAPWORLorien/Desc
"This forest, also known as the Golden Wood for its Mallorn Trees, is the home of Galadriel and Celeborn of the Elves.\n\n Size: 400 x 300\n Lairs: 3x Goblin Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost"
END

Map:MAPWORLostriand
"Lostriand"
END

Map:MAPWORLostriand/Desc
"Lands found between Amon Sul and Rivendell that are dominated by the Weather Hills.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 2x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPWORMinasMorgul
"Minas Morgul"
END

Map:MAPWORMinasMorgul/Desc
"Also known as the Tower of Sorcery, this dark fortress was held by the leader of the Ringwraiths during the War of the Ring.\n\n Size: 450 x 450\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair\n Neutral Structures: 3x Outpost, 1x Signal Fire, Fortress"
END

