OBJECT:HordeMordorSoldiersOfRhun
"Easterlings"
END

MAP:MapMPEnedwaithII
"Morthond Valley"
END

Map:MAPMPMorthondValley/Desc
"The Morthond was one of the seven rivers of Gondor. Aragorn, Gimli, Legolas, and the Army of the Dead exited from the Paths of the Dead alongside it\n\n Size: 320 x 380\n Lairs: 2x Spider Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPRhunShore
"Dwarrowdelf"
END

Map:MAPMPDwarrowdelf/Desc
"Khazad-dum, also known as Hadhodrond, Casarrondo and Phurunargian, which translates to Dwarrowdelf, latterly known as Moria.\n\n Size: 600 x 500\n Lairs: 8x Goblin Lair, 4x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Outpost, 4x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

MAP:MapMPKhamulTomb
"Lebennin"
END

Map:MAPMPLebennin/Desc
"This lush, green land in southern Gondor lies where the Anduin River completes its journey into the Bay of Belfalas.\n\n Size: 425 x 500\n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 6x Warg Lair, 4x Goblin Lair \n Neutral Structures: 3x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPWestRohan
"West Emnet"
END

Map:MAPMPWestEmnet/Desc
"Grassy lands of Rohan, lying between the Entwash and the Isen River.\n\n Size: 313 x 385\n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Warg Lair, 2x Goblin Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPAmonHen
"Amon Hen"
END

Map:MAPMPAmonHen/Desc
"A hill in the Emyn Muil at Nen Hithoel's west. At its summit was the Seat of Seeing, a ruined structure by the late Third Age. \n\n Size: 390 x 415 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPChetwood
"Chetwood"
END

Map:MAPMPChetwood/Desc
"This forest situated east of Bree was bordered by the Midgewater marshes to the east, and the Great Eastern Road to the south. Aragorn led the hobbits through this forest on their way to Rivendell. \n\n Size: 360 x 325 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPColdfells
"Coldfells"
END

Map:MAPMPColdfells/Desc
"Once part of the kingdom of Rhudaur, these hills are now wild and dangerous. Many trolls lurk in the area. \n\n Size: 450 x 450 \n Lairs: Troll x5 \n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPDimrilldale
"Dimrill Dale"
END

Map:MAPMPDimrilldale/Desc
"This valley east of Moria was the final battleground of the War of the Dwarves and Orcs. \n\n Size: 420 x 350 \n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair"
END

Map:MAPMPEredlithui
"Ered Lithui"
END

Map:MAPMPEredlithui/Desc
"Ered Lithui or the Mountains of Ash form the northern border of Mordor. The road that runs east along them is used exclusively by Easterlings loyal to the Great Eye. \n\n Size: 420 x 375 \n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair"
END

Map:MAPMPPlateauofGorgoroth
"Plateau of Gorgoroth"
END

Map:MAPMPPlateauofGorgoroth/Desc
"A deadly, barren region covered in ash and fumes \n\n Size: 500 x 500 \n Neutral structures: 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPSirannon
"This once tumultuous river flows from the Gates of Durin to Ost-in-Edhil, the ruined elf city of Eregion. \n\n Size: 350 x 350 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x War Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPFirienDale
"Firien Dale"
END

Map:MAPMPFirienDale/Desc
"A deep cleft separating the Halifirien hill from its spur of the White Mountains, the source of the Mering Stream. \n\n Size: 410 x 315 \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPMeringStream
"Mering Stream"
END

Map:MAPMPMeringStream/Desc
"The Mering Stream was known for being one of borders between the kingdoms of Gondor and Rohan. The stream rises in the Firien-Dale, flows through the Firien wood and bends eastward through the marshes of the Fenmarch. \n\n Size: 380 x 340 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPSouthHollin
"Marshes of Midgewater"
END

Map:MAPMPMarshesofMidgewater/Desc
"An area within Bree-land in the south-eastern region. It is known for its treacherous bogs that extend as far as the Weather Hills. \n\n Size: 500 x 500 \n Lairs: 2x Spider Lair, 2x Troll Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPSouthEnedwaith
"South Enedwaith"
END

Map:MAPMPSouthEnedwaith/Desc
"A mountainous region between the river Gwathlo and the coast of the Belegaer sea. \n\n Size: 550 x 600 \n Lairs: 5x Troll Lair, 4x Warg Lair, 4x Goblin Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPHarnenOasis
"Harnen Oasis"
END

Map:MAPMPHarnenOasis/Desc
"A vast oasis located north of the Harnen Valley \n\n Size: 525 x 525 \n Lairs: 4x Troll Lair, 2x Goblin Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPSorrowIsles
"Sorrow Isles"
END

Map:MAPMPSorrowIsles/Desc
"A group of lone Islands in the Sea of Belfalas. It is said to be the prison of two evil spirits who drive the island's unsuspecting visitors into madness. \n\n Size: 470 x 470 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Goblin Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Signal Fire, 2x Shipwright"
END

Map:MAPWORDunland
"Dunland"
END

Map:MAPWORDunland/Desc
"The Eastern regions of the Enedwaith, home of the Wild Men, sworn enemies of Rohan.\n\n Size: 450 x 450 \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 1x Ruined Tower"
END

Map:MAPWORIronHills
"Iron Hills"
END

Map:MAPWORIronHills/Desc
"These hills, rich in Iron, were long held by the Dwarves and Dain Ironfoot.\n\n Size: 368 x 338 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Spider Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPNorthWold
"North Wold"
END

Map:MAPMPNorthWold/Desc
"An old, desolate area to the north of the Summit of Amon Hen. \n\n Size: 460 x 460 \n Lairs: 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPEmynSul
"Emyn Sul"
END

Map:MAPMPEmynSul/Desc
"Otherwise known as Weather Hills, Emyn Sul was a hilly region north of the Great East Road between Bree and Mitheithel, at one time the boundry between Arthedain and Rhudaur. \n \n Size: 600 x 450 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair , 2x Goblin Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPBaranduin
"River Baranduin"
END

Map:MAPMPBaranduin/Desc
"The Baranduin River of Eriador is known by the Hobbits as the Brandywine River. It marks the the boundary between the known and the unknown. \n\n Size: 500 x 500 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 4x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures:"
END

Map:MAPMPBrandyHills
"East Carrock"
END

Map:MAPMPEastCarrock/Desc
"The Carrock was a stony eyot in the upper reaches of the River Anduin, to the north of the Old Ford. The river looped around the rock although there was a ford of stones to the eastern bank, while there was a swirling channel under its western cliff. \n\n Size: 352 x 416 \n Lairs: 4x Warg Lair, 2x Goblin Lair \n Neutral Structures:"
END

Map:MAPMPEnchantedRiver
"Enchanted River"
END

Map:MAPMPEnchantedRiver/Desc
"The Enchanted River was a black river in Mirkwood that flowed north from its source in the Mountains of Mirkwood towards the Forest River. \n\n Size: 420 x 308 \n Lairs: 2x Drake Lair, 4x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPGardensofFarHarad
"Gladden Fields"
END

Map:MAPMPGladdenFields/Desc
"The Gladden Fields were a marshland located in the vale of the Gladden river, and on the banks of the river Anduin. It was there that the One Ring was lost by Isildur, and found again centuries later by Deagol the Stoor. \n\n Size: 460 x 396 \n Lairs: 5x Warg Lair, 4x Goblin Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPHarrowdale
"Harrowdale"
END

Map:MAPMPHarrowdale/Desc
"Harrowdale was a deep, north-south valley cut out of the White Mountains by the Snowbourn river in Rohan. \n At its southern end, between the mountains known as the Starkhorn and Irensaga, stood Dunharrow, a great clifftop refuge of the Rohirrim. \n\n Size: 460 x 462 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPSouthMeringStream
"Mering Stream II"
END

Map:MAPMPSouthMeringStream/Desc
"The Great West Road crosses the Mering Stream, a border river that separates Rohan and Gondor. \n\n Size: 380 x 340 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPNumenorsDownfall
"Twilit Shores"
END

Map:MAPMPTwilitShores/Desc
"Lost in the seas of Tol Eressea, the Twilit isles have been said to be nearly unnavigable by mortal men \n\n Size: 600 x 600 \n Lairs: 2x Drake Lair, 2x Troll Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire, 4x Outpost, 6x Shipwright"
END

Map:MAPMPCardolanHighlands
"Cardolan Highlands"
END

Map:MAPMPCardolanHighlands/Desc
"Cardolan was a realm once part of the Dunedain Kingdom of Arnor. The borders of Cardolan extended from the River Brandywine to the west, the River Hoarwell to the east, and the River Greyflood to the south. \n\n Size: 378 x 378 \n Lairs: 1x Troll Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair, 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPOldFord
"Old Ford"
END

Map:MAPMPOldFord/Desc
"The Old Ford was the point where the Old Forest Road crossed the River Anduin, about forty miles downriver from the Carrock. In older times, the river was crossed by a stone bridge here, but by the end of the Third Age, the bridge had long since disappeared, and the crossing was no more than a simple ford. \n\n Size: 500 x 500 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Spider Lair, 2x Goblin Lair, 6x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 4x Inn, 2x Signal Fire, 2x Outpost"
END

Map:MAPMPGladdenRiver
"Gladden River"
END

Map:MAPMPGladdenRiver/Desc
"The Gladden, also referred to as River Goldwater by the Elves, was a short but important river of the Vales of Anduin. \n\n Size: 378 x 342 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures:"
END

Map:MAPMPPazghar
"Pazghar"
END

Map:MAPMPPazghar/Desc
"The Oasis of Pazghar, the great city of East Harad \n\n Size: 490 x 490 \n Lairs: 8x Spider Lair, 5x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPBrandyHillsCanyon
"Brandy Hills Canyon"
END

Map:MAPMPBrandyHillsCanyon/Desc
"This is an area north of Buckland along the eastern shores of Brandywine River until the Brandywood. Girdley Island is the only named point of interest of these hills though they are dotted by small Arnorian ruins. Some young hunters may be seen hunting bears and boars taking shelter in those ruins. \n\n Size: 500 x 500 \n Lairs: 1x Barrow Wight Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPWoodmenTown
"Woodmen Town"
END

Map:MAPMPWoodmenTown/Desc
"The oldest settlement of the Woodmen was founded by the folk of Balthi long ago. He brought the Lamp out of the darkness, and the light of the Lamp has ever protected Woodmen-town and its inhabitants. The town nestles on the banks of the Enchanted River, which blocks attacks from the east. The Woodmen also use the river to travel back and forth between Woodmen-town and Woodland Hall. \n\n Size: 404 x 404 \n Lairs: 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

MAP:MapMPHaradOasisii
"Anfalas"
END

Map:MAPMPAnfalas/Desc
"The western coastal section of Gondor populated by small villages of herdsmen and fishermen.\n\n Size: 450 x 450\n Lairs: 4x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPAnfalasII
"Anfalas Shores"
END

Map:MAPMPAnfalasII/Desc
"The Anfalas, or Long Shore, also known in Westron as the Langstrand or the Strand, lay between the rivers Lefnui and Morthond, south of the Pinnath Gelin.\n\n Size: 360 x 390\n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Inn, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPAnorienII
"Upper Anorien"
END

Map:MAPMPAnorienII/Desc
"Buckland Fields"
END

Map:MAPMPBucklandII/Desc
"The Eastern border of the Shire was home of Merry Brandybuck.\n\n Size: 330 x 360\n Lairs: 4x Barrow Wight Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPRhudaurII
"Upper Rhudaur"
END

Map:MAPMPRhudaurII/Desc
"The rolling terrain of Rhudaur has always proved to be a ready battleground for the local hillmen and their invading enemies.\n\n Size: 500 x 350\n Lairs:\n Neutral Structures: 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPIronHillsII
"Central Iron Hills"
END

Map:MAPMPIronHillsII/Desc
"A mineral rich region which is the source of the River Redwater, the name given to the river for the reddish iron particles found in its water.\n\n Size: 600 x 535\n Lairs: 7x Spider Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost, 1x Inn, 1x Signal Fire, 2x Fortress"
END

Map:MAPMPIronHillsIII
"North Iron Hills"
END

Map:MAPMPIronHillsIII/Desc
"A range of mountains located in northern Middle-earth. It is the realm of the Dwarves of Durin's Folk.\n\n Size: 498 x 398\n Lairs: 8x Spider Lair, 2x Fire Drake Lair, 4x Destructible Environment\n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPIronHillsIV
"Lower Iron Hills"
END

Map:MAPMPIronHillsIV/Desc
"A mineral rich region which is the source of the River Redwater, the name given to the river for the reddish iron particles found in its water.\n\n Size: 550 x 550\n Lairs: 4x Spider Lair, 2x Fire Drake Lair, 10x Destructible Environment\n Neutral Structures: 4x Outpost, 2x Inn, 2x Signal Fire"
END

MAP:MAPMPIronHillsV
"Iron Hills Outskirts"
END

MAP:MAPMPIronHillsV/Desc
"These hills, rich in Iron, were long held by the Dwarves and Dain Ironfoot.\n\n Size: 600 x 600\n Lairs: 8x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost"
END

Map:MAPMPMountGundabadII
"Central Mount Gundabad"
END

Map:MAPMPMountGundabadII/Desc
"The icy passages of Mount Gundabad have seen countless battles between the local Orc tribes and their foes.\n\n Size: 500 x 500\n Lairs: 4x Goblin Lair\n Neutral Structures: 4x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPTombsOfKarnaII
"Lower Tombs of Karna"
END

Map:MAPMPTombsOfKarnaII/Desc
"Chosen for their fertility and beauty, these oasis spots serve as gravesites for the rulers of Far Harad.\n\n Size: 360 x 380\n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPTombsOfKarnaIII
"Upper Tombs of Karna"
END

Map:MAPMPTombsOfKarnaIII/Desc
"Central Tombs of Karna"
END

Map:MAPMPTombsOfKarnaIV/Desc
"Eastfold Plains"
END

MAP:MAPMPEastfoldII/Desc
"The eastern lands of Rohan, bordering Gondor.\n\n Size: 455 x 390\n Lairs: 6x Goblin Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 1x Outpost"
END

Map:MAPMPTowerHillsII
"Upper Tower Hills"
END

Map:MAPMPTowerHillsII/Desc
"These hills are the home of the ancient Elven towers that held the Elendil Stone, the last of the Palantiri of the North.\n\n Size: 315 x 375\n Lairs: 2x Goblin Lair, 2x Warg Lair, 2x Troll Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 2x Tower"
END

