END

OBJECT:MordorTavernDescription
"Eastfarthing Hills"
END

Map:MAPMPEastfarthingHills/Desc
"The Eastfarthing was one of the four Farthings of the Shire. Its westernmost point was the Three-Farthing Stone, its eastern border was the Brandywine River, and its southern border was the River Shirebourn. \n\n Size: 500 x 500 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 4x Warg Lair, 2x Goblin Lair \n Neutral Structures: 4x Inn , 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPEastEmnetPlains
"East Emnet Plains"
END

Map:MAPMPEastEmnetPlains/Desc
"The Eastemnet was a part of Rohan, and an area of wide, grassy plains found east of the river Entwash, between it and the Great River Anduin. \n\n Size: 450 x 450 \n Lairs: 4x Troll Lair, 4x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn , 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPPinnathGelin
"Pinnath Gelin"
END

Map:MAPMPPinnathGelin/Desc
"Pinnath Gelin or Green Hills was a fief in the far west of Gondor, bounded to the west by the River Lefnui, and to the east by the Morthond. \n\n Size: 400 x 460 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 4x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn , 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPDorEnErnil
"Dor-en-Ernil"
END

Map:MAPMPDorEnErnil/Desc
"Though its boundaries are not clearly established, Dor-en-Ernil appears to have been part of - or perhaps synonymous with - the mountainous coastland fief known as Belfalas or the wider sense of Dol Amroth. \n\n Size: 550 x 570 \n Lairs: 5x Troll Lair, 6x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Inn"
END

