Map:MAPMPNorthernWaste
"Northern Waste"
END

Map:MAPMPNorthernWaste/Desc
"Also known as Forodwaith, the Northern Waste was a vast, cold region in the far north end of Middle-earth, beyond the Mountains of Angmar, Mount Gundabad, and the Ered Mithrin. \n\n Size: 500 x 500 \n Lairs: 4x Troll Lair, 4x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire, 2x Inn, 2x Outpost"
END

Map:MAPMPNorthernWasteII
"Northern Waste II"
END

Map:MAPMPNorthernWasteII/Desc
"Also known as Forodwaith, the Northern Waste was a vast, cold region in the far north end of Middle-earth, beyond the Mountains of Angmar, Mount Gundabad, and the Ered Mithrin. \n\n Size: 500 x 500 \n Lairs: 4x Troll Lair, 4x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire, 2x Inn, 1x Outpost"
END

Map:MAPMPUmbarPeninsula
"Umbar Peninsula"
END

Map:MAPMPUmbarPeninsula/Desc
"A peninsula north-west of the City of the Corsairs. \n\n Size: 500 x 500 \n Lairs: 3x Troll Lair, 1x Barrow Wight Lair, 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire, 2x Inn, 1x Outpost"
END

Map:MAPMPSouthMirkwood
"South Mirkwood"
END

Map:MAPMPSouthMirkwood/Desc
"A dark, hilly region in the south of Mirkwood. \n\n Size: 400 x 400 \n Lairs: 2x Spider Lair, 2x Warg Lair, 2x Barrow Wight Lair"
END

Map:MAPMPSeaofNurnen
"Sea of Nurnen"
END

Map:MAPMPSeaofNurnen/Desc
"The lands around the Sea of Nurnen are lush and thriving. It is here, far from the smokes of Orodruin, where countless men work the fields for the armies of the Dark Lord.\n\n Size: 500 x 400\n Lairs: 2x Warg Lair, 2x Wight Lair\n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPBree
"Bree"
END

Map:MAPMPBree/Desc
"A village of Men and Hobbits, located east of the Shire and south of Fornost in Eriador.\n\n Size: 500 x 500 \n Lairs: 4x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPBeleriand
"Beleriand"
END

Map:MAPMPBeleriand/Desc
"At the end of the First Age of Middle-earth, Beleriand was broken in the War of Wrath by the the Maiar, against Morgoth. As the inhabitants fled much of Beleriand sank in the sea. The left behind souls still fight their battle for supremancy of the sunken lands.\n\n Size: 400 x 400 \n Lairs: 3x Troll Lair, 3x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 3x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPEavesofFangorn
"Eaves of Fangorn"
END

Map:MAPMPEavesofFangorn/Desc
"The Eaves of Fangorn is an area within East Rohan. It is a remnant of the once great Fangorn Forest. \n\n Size: 421 x 360 \n Lairs: 3x Troll Lair, 3x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 3x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPForlond
"Forlond"
END

Map:MAPMPForlond/Desc
"Forlond was a harbour that lay on the northern shore of the Gulf of Lune, in the Elvish land of Forlindon. It had a counterpart on the southern shore: the Harlond. Forlond was located at the mouth of an unnamed river that traversed Forlindon, some two hundred miles to the northwest of the Grey Havens. \n\n Size: 450 x 450 \n Lairs: 5x Troll Lair"
END

Map:MAPMPHillsofEvendim
"Hills of Evendim"
END

Map:MAPMPHillsofEvendim/Desc
"The Hills of Evendim, or Emyn Uial in Sindarin, were a series of hills in northern Eriador. \n\n Size: 500 x 550 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Spider Lair, 1x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Inn, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPIcebayofForochel
"Icebay of Forochel"
END

Map:MAPMPIcebayofForochel/Desc
"An immense body of water located north of Eriador and northwest of Forodwaith in the cold, northern regions of Middle-earth. A strip of land called the Cape of Forochel formed the western boundary of the bay, creating a narrow entrance to the south. \n\n Size: 550 x 550 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 4x Warg Lair, 4x Goblin Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPIsleofRhun
"Isle of Rhun"
END

Map:MAPMPIsleofRhun/Desc
"A palmy isle located in the south-eastern part of the Sea of Rhun. \n\n Size: 500 x 500 \n Lairs: 3x Troll Lair, 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 2x Inn, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPLaketown
"Lake-town"
END

Map:MAPMPLaketown/Desc
"Lake-town, also referred to as Esgaroth, was a small independent settlement of Men in the north-western part of the Long Lake in Rhovanion. \n\n Size: 600 x 520 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Warg Lair, 5x Goblin Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Outpost, 1x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPLune
"Lune"
END

Map:MAPMPLune/Desc
"The river Lune is a river of north-western Eriador. The Grey Havens lie at the mouth of this river. \n\n Size: 350 x 350 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPTumladenValley
"Tumladen Valley"
END

Map:MAPMPTumladenValley/Desc
"A hidden valley within the Encircling Mountains where the Elven city of Gondolin was built during the First Age. \n\n Size: 550 x 550 \n Lairs: 3x Troll Lair, 4x Spider Lair, 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 4x Inn, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPTumladen
"Pass of Tumladen"
END

Map:MAPMPTumladen/Desc
"Tumladen is a deep valley between the rivers Celos and Sirith. It was the refuge of many civilians from Minas Tirith during the War of the Ring. \n\n Size: 490 x 460 \n Lairs: 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 1x Signal Fire"
END

Map:MAPMPUpperAnduin
"Upper Anduin"
END

Map:MAPMPUpperAnduin/Desc
"The Anduin flows from northern reaches of Middle-Earth to the bay of Belfalas, far to the south. The ancestors of the Rohirrim lived near the springs of the Great River. \n\n Size: 400 x 400 \n Lairs: 1x Troll Lair, 4x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 1x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPStockbrook
"Fords of Stockbrook"
END

Map:MAPMPStockbrook/Desc
"The Stockbrook was a stream located in the Eastfarthing of the Shire. It joined the Brandywine after passing its namesake, the village of Stock. It had steep banks lined with brambles that gradually become lower as it heads towards the river. \n\n Size: 313 x 375 \n Lairs: 2x Barrow Wight Lair, 4x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn"
END

Map:MAPMPHobbitonHill
"Hobbiton Hill"
END

Map:MAPMPHobbitonHill/Desc
"Hobbiton Hill, sometimes referred to as The Hill, was a hill in the Westfarthing between Hobbiton and Overhill. \n\n Size: 402 x 400 \n Lairs: 2x Troll Lair, 2x Warg Lair \n Neutral Structures: 2x Inn, 1x Signal Fire"
END

